-- check/bad: §3.3's last clause. Derivation needs a shape to walk, and a
-- `foreign type` has no constructors — so `compare` on one resolves only
-- through §3.2's table or through a `pub compare` in its declaring module,
-- and `List` has neither until §5.2 gives it one in S6. `unknown_method`,
-- not a silently derived function over a representation the compiler
-- cannot see.
--
-- `==` on the same value still works, through the `equatable` marker that
-- §3.4 says means exactly "has an `eq`" — the bridge core leans on until
-- S6, and §11 carries it as that slice's obligation.
pub sortish : List Int, List Int -> Bool
sortish a b =
    a < b
